- We did it!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.853
We made it through our first
week of this show together!

00:00:14.094 --> 00:00:17.770
(audience applauding)
(screams)

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.270
I don't think I've ever had
this much fun in my entire life

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.750
and I hope that you have
enjoyed this week too.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.920
That's the whole point of all of this.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.950
Let's turn to our virtual
friends and family, our VFFs.

00:00:32.007 --> 00:00:34.766
(audience applauding)

00:00:34.766 --> 00:00:36.554
How fun is that?

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:38.720
Emily, can I ask you a question?

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.573
Who is your favorite guest this week?

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.580
- I loved her interview with Shirley's,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.730
it was so natural and organic,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.620
and part of a genuine
conversation, I loved it.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.010
- Oh, I'm so happy to hear that.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.240
It's so nice to hear feedback, you know,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.180
it gives us a sense of
what people are liking

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.170
or connecting to, it's really important.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.340
Thank you for sharing, I mean it.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.330
You know what, spoiler alert!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.083
All of the guests were my favorite.

00:01:06.082 --> 00:01:07.970
(audience applauding)
Okay.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.360
It's true.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.300
I'm so excited for today's guest too.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.146
Billy Porter is here and he is nominated

00:01:16.146 --> 00:01:18.160
(audience applauding)
for another Emmy this weekend.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.240
In fact, I even wore this outfit for him

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.680
because I mean, he is the king of style.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.950
Also today, the mom
behind this viral photo

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.760
opens up about her son's struggle

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.840
with distance learning,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.180
something a lot of us can relate to.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.800
This photo went crazy and
we get to talk to her today.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.733
But first let's get into some Drew's News.

00:01:41.696 --> 00:01:43.107
(audience applauding)

00:01:43.107 --> 00:01:44.356
(car brakes screeching)
(glass shattering)

00:01:44.356 --> 00:01:45.289
(cat meowing)

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:48.047
(upbeat music)

00:01:48.047 --> 00:01:51.901
Excuse me, sir! mom! Guy!

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.484
Tell me your story!

00:01:55.461 --> 00:01:57.794
Mom, I asked you a question.

00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:03.232
This is Drew's News!

00:02:03.232 --> 00:02:05.395
This is Drew's News.

00:02:05.395 --> 00:02:06.745
It's Drew's News!

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:08.283
(bright music)
(audience applauding)

00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:09.210
(hands clapping)

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:13.550
Fun fact, the dog in the
Drew's News monologue opener,

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.890
that's Lucy, my dog.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.990
Alright, now let's see
what made the papers.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.410
Okay, first up the Deseret News

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.690
reports on a new study from Brigham young,

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.260
looking at why girls love
Disney princesses so much.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.020
They surveyed a large group of girls

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.700
and found that they connected
to them for four reasons.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.520
Okay, their virtues,
they're royalty, (sneers)

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.660
their aspirational lives, okay,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.920
and their rebellious spirits.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.383
Hm.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.563
I can relate to that last one.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.630
So can my daughter, Olive.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.463
Trust me.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.440
The thing about this, though,
that really speaks to me

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.117
is it reminds me of a
movie called "Ever After".

00:03:02.117 --> 00:03:05.210
(audience applauds)

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.760
Thanks guys.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.690
The reason "Ever After" changed my life

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.590
is because as a girl, we read fairytales

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.220
and we're a little conditioned
to wait to be rescued

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.610
and this film totally flipped
the script pun intended

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.060
on that for me.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.270
It's like, we still want
love at the end of the day,

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.420
you still want the prince, you
still want all the romance,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.710
but the point is to get yourself there.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:31.710
And for me to have that
revelation in my early twenties,

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.980
that we don't wait to be
rescued, we rescue ourselves,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.290
well, it changed the entire course

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.550
of the rest of my professional
and personal life.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.290
And I just wanna thank Disney

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.850
because I think you've
really modernized fairytales

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.480
for young girls out there.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.810
We no longer wait to be rescued.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:52.170
We do want love and the
Prince at the end of the day,

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.270
don't get us wrong, but you've shown us

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:59.110
that we can dream big
princess and be capable

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.350
and we need stories that
remind us of just that.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.656
So thank you.

00:04:03.656 --> 00:04:07.175
(audience applauding)
(hands clapping)

00:04:07.175 --> 00:04:08.520
So, okay.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.630
In transition, our next story requires you

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.110
to loosen that belt buckle

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.886
cause it's some time for food news.

00:04:15.886 --> 00:04:17.840
(audience applauding)

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.690
Okay.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.120
This story totally spoke to me

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.077
because my girls gets
so excited when I say,

00:04:23.077 --> 00:04:25.230
"We're going to the gas station."

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.660
It's kind of their favorite place to eat.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.560
It's true, come on, there's
so many treats and snacks,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.450
they love it.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.560
So check this out, girls.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.490
7-11 is getting in on the action

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.170
with the new line of
Autumnal Sandwich Cookies.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.190
They've got pumpkin spice,
they've got salted caramel,

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:45.656
they've even got ye old candy corn.

00:04:45.656 --> 00:04:46.770
(audience laughing)

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:51.491
All sold by the sleeve, and
I've got some right here.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.350
(paper rustling)

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.530
That's right.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:55.440
Apparently this is called the sleeve.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.870
I just learned that too.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.250
All right, let's taste
test the candy corn,

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.610
ye old candy corn.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.620
Oh hey, VFFs?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.200
Nathan, Ashley, you want to
get it on, on the action?

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.870
I heard you ran out to
7-11 and picked some up

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.350
to taste test with me.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.400
- Hi Drew!

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.560
Yeah, we just got back.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.030
We got some candy corn,
we can't wait to try it.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.730
- And also pumpkin spice.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.210
- Cheers, cookie cheers.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.043
What do you guys think?

00:05:20.043 --> 00:05:22.300
- Not bad.
- Yeah, I think they taste

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.050
pretty much exactly like candy corn,

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.110
maybe a little bit
sweeter, but they're great.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.270
- I definitely taste the
pumpkin, not as much spice,

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.743
but it's good.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.740
- I'm gonna say winner
winner chicken dinner.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.930
I'm in and thank you, Nathan and Ashley

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.172
for being culinary guinea pigs with me.

00:05:37.172 --> 00:05:38.980
(hands clapping)
Okay.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.065
Now it is time for our
Drew's News astrology report.

00:05:43.065 --> 00:05:45.648
(upbeat music)

00:05:47.812 --> 00:05:49.310
(hands clapping)

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.870
So, here to help us read the stars

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.293
is astrologer extraordinaire, Aliza Kelly.

00:05:55.293 --> 00:05:56.640
(audience applauding)
(hands clapping)

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.010
Hi Aliza!

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:01.590
- Drew, thank you so much for
having me, congratulations.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.690
- Thank you so much, I--

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:03.964
- [Eliza] This is so exciting.

00:06:03.964 --> 00:06:05.880
- It is, it is.
- It's so exciting.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.100
- And it's like first week, done, got it.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.260
Okay, here we go.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.920
And we get to go into the weekend with you

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.620
and I wanna ask September,
what's going on?

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.410
Well, you launched at the perfect time

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:23.670
because we are actually in a
transitional moment right now.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:27.560
So on September 22nd, we
are beginning Libra season.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.950
It's the autumn Equinox.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.610
So we're moving into a
reflective, thoughtful energy.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.240
We're gonna see a little less sun,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.890
but this means that we're
gonna be our own sun.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.000
We're going to generate our own radiance

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.630
and we're going to learn
to understand ourselves

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.340
from a different perspective.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.600
- Aliza, can I ask you
what a birth chart is?

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.220
- It is basically a snapshot of the sky

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.180
at someone's or some
thing's exact time of birth.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.540
So using the birth chart,

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.580
we could see the rising,
the sun and the moon,

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:00.410
and we can really understand
who that person is

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.610
or if it's an event, what that person

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.550
or what that event is all about.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.740
- Well, speaking of birth charts,

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.450
I heard you maybe have a surprise for us?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:10.700
- I do, I do.
(screaming)

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.020
Okay, so I know that
this is your launch week.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.690
I know that you just
launched on September 14th.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.500
So I decided to look at the astrology

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.060
for the Drew Barrymore show.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.510
- It's like having a birth chart

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:26.470
for basically my third child.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.400
- Yes.
- Okay, tell us what is it?

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.750
- So you have a beautiful third child.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.520
The third child is a Libra rising.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:38.270
So this is perfect, it's
beautiful, it's about balance,

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.430
it's about harmony, it's about symmetry

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.890
and it's also a very social energy.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.820
So it's about sharing the stage.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.230
It's about you giving
basically a space for others

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.800
to be able to share their stories too.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.040
It's all about that scales of balance.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.850
- Oh my gosh, that's exactly
what our mission is here.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:56.920
- It's perfect.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.880
- Okay, wait.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.600
Okay, what about our rising sun?

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.780
- So the sun is a Virgo for
the Drew Barrymore show,

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:06.010
and what I really love about
this is that you are a Pisces.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.960
- I am.
- And Virgo and Pisces

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.530
are opposite signs,

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.030
but opposite in astrology

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.510
is actually a very wonderful thing

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.740
because it means the goal is the same,

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.300
just different ways of getting there.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.740
So you and the show are
basically have the same mission,

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:24.040
which is how can I make
the world a better place?

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.232
- And how about the moon?

00:08:26.232 --> 00:08:27.645
(imitates wolf howl)

00:08:27.645 --> 00:08:30.107
(Aliza laughing)

00:08:30.107 --> 00:08:33.310
- Yes, so the moon is
also a very important part

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.370
of the astrology.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.550
It is sort of what's
going on on the inside.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.550
It is the emotional inner world

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.550
and in this case, it's really showing us

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:44.010
the backbone of the show and it's Leo,

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.200
which is all about
entertaining and theatricality

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.800
and passion and really having fun.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.150
So at the end of the day,
we're going to find balance,

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:56.810
we're going to help people,
we're gonna use communication

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.210
and we're also gonna have a great time

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.680
and look fabulous while we're doing it.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.472
So that's a pretty good
chart, I would say.

00:09:02.472 --> 00:09:03.980
(audience applauding)
(Aliza laughing)

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:04.870
- Aliza!

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:05.703
- [Aliza] It's a good chart

00:09:05.703 --> 00:09:07.170
- And you know what I did?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.260
I hope it's okay not to
add more onto your plate,

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.940
but I asked my mom if she would give me

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:17.120
the exact time I was born, it's 11:51 AM

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.670
and I've never had my chart done.

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:20.530
Could I--
- You haven't?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.180
- Ah ah.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.350
- Oh my goodness, we have
to do this right now.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.360
- Could I ask you to do my chart,

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:30.070
and we could come back on
the show and talk about it?

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.400
- It's a yes from me.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.466
It's a big yes, right here.
- Thank you!

00:09:33.466 --> 00:09:36.426
Thank you, thank you, thank
you I really appreciate it.

00:09:36.426 --> 00:09:39.009
(bright music)

